An earlier attempt at this task stopped before it was done. <%= out_of_steps ? "It used all of its tool calls." : "It stopped calling tools without calling finish." %> This is a new conversation, but its changes are still in the repository: build on them and do not start again.

The task, as planned:
<%= task %>

<% if request -%>
The whole feature request this task is one part of. Take exact values, names and text from it; build only this task's part:
<%= request %>

<% end -%>
<% unless done.empty? -%>
Tasks already done in this run:
<% done.each do |d| -%>
- <%= d %>
<% end -%>

<% end -%>
<% if files.empty? -%>
It changed no files.

<% else -%>
Files it changed: <%= files.join(", ") %>

<% end -%>
<% if diff -%>
Its changes:
<%= diff %>

<% end -%>
<% if calls -%>
Its last tool calls. Do not repeat what did not work:
<%= calls %>

<% end -%>
<% if last_words -%>
Its last message:
<%= last_words %>

<% end -%>
<% if checks -%>
The harness ran the task's checks just now:
<%= checks %>

Do only what these results and the task still need. Add nothing else.
<% else -%>
Find what is still missing and do only that. Run the checks that apply.
<% end -%>
The task ends only when you call the finish tool. Saying that you are done in a message does not finish it.
